# Template for the environment variables this app needs.
#
# Local dev:  copy this file to ".env.local" and fill in real values.
# Vercel:     add the same keys under Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
#
# JSONBin.io backs the runtime cloud database. These are used server-side only
# (in lib/db.ts) and are never exposed to the browser.
#
# Tip: use a SEPARATE bin per environment — same JSONBIN_ACCESS_KEY, different
# JSONBIN_BIN_ID (e.g. one bin for local, another for Vercel). A fresh/empty
# Vercel bin auto-initializes itself with the seed (data/crm-seed.json) on first
# load, so it can start empty or already hold the persistent data.
#
# IMPORTANT — the access key contains "$" characters. In .env.local you must
# escape each "$" as "\$" so Next's env loader keeps it literal. In the Vercel
# dashboard, paste the RAW value (e.g. $2a$10$...) with no escaping.

JSONBIN_BIN_ID=your-bin-id
JSONBIN_ACCESS_KEY=your-access-key
